/**
 * Official product marks, inlined as data URLs so the Electron file:// build needs no asset-path resolution.
 *
 * Brand tiles come from LobeHub's official icon set (MIT):
 *   https://github.com/lobehub/lobe-icons  ->  @lobehub/icons-static-avatar/avatars/<slug>.webp
 *   brand page: https://lobehub.com/zh/icons/hermesagent
 * Vendor originals + the exact slug manifest are archived in assets/official-brand/lobehub/.
 * Three brands override the LobeHub tile with the vendor original the user supplied
 * (archived in assets/official-brand/user-provided/):
 *   Hermes   -> Hermes Agent desktop app resources/icon.ico (white tile, full-bleed girl)
 *   DeepSeek -> DeepSeek Harness resources/tray.ico (dark whale on a plain white tile)
 *   OpenAI   -> ChatGPT black knot #000, the same path as OpenAIMark (no black square)
 * Codex uses that same OpenAI knot (not the LobeHub cloud). Doubao keeps the artwork
 * from before the LobeHub sweep, archived in user-provided/restored/.
 * GitHub Copilot uses GitHub's own octocat mark (Simple Icons CC0 path, white on the
 * same dark rounded tile) instead of the old Copilot robot face, which reads as a pig
 * head at small sizes. Archived as user-provided/restored/github-octocat-64.png.
 * The DeepSeek whale and the OpenAI knot are enlarged so they read at 14px.
 * The 64px tiles here are those originals with rounded corners only; no redraws, no recolouring.
 * Project-specific marks (zcode, droid, metaMuse, museCode, customAcp) are kept as-is.
 *
 * A name match beats the driver mark: a bridged CLI (WorkBuddy/CodeBuddy) runs on the Claude
 * driver but is its own product, so it must not borrow Anthropic's star.
 */
/**
 * One source of truth: every official LobeHub tile used by the renderer. Components such as
 * HermesMark / DeepSeekMark / CodexMark point at these constants so brand marks stay identical
 * in the engine list, the driver chips and the avatar picker.
 */
